WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
A connected field: aerial observation, a fixed station and
ground inspection.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Station raises its mast, opens the bay and prepares the scissor
platform.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:57.000
The drone takes off and surveys the plot. Camera views and
readings are simulated.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:12.000
NDVI uses synthetic red and NIR bands. Local differences guide
the inspection.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:34.000
WALL-AI deploys its drone to inspect the local area with RGB and
thermal views.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:50.000
First INSECE sample: moisture, temperature, pH, conductivity and
N/P/K.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:02:06.000
The onboard cameras observe the surroundings on the way to the
second location.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:22.000
The robot stops, inserts its probe and records the second
sample.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:40.000
WALL-AI travels through another part of the vineyard with its
onboard cameras.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:56.000
Third sample: seven parameters linked to their location and
acquisition time.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:13.000
The robot returns with its probe retracted. Three samples and
imagery are ready for review.
